{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302202-the-triad-and-the-spheres-which-could-govern-what","id":1302202,"title":"The Triad and the Spheres - Which could govern what?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-03T07:37:28-07:00","id":1302202,"title":"The Triad and the Spheres - Which could govern what?","content":"<i>This post was inspired by another forum topic and I decided to make my own instead of derail the original thread.<br /> __________________________________________________ _________________________________________</i><br /> <br /> I liked the thought of matching the 9 spheres to the metaphysical Triad just for fun. The Wyrm, Weaver, and Wyld. I thought each would/could govern three spheres. Perhaps there could be a belief system (if it doesn't exist) for Mages to adopt and shape it into a Foundation, Paradigm, yada yada.<br /> <br /> Wyld - Matter, Spirit, Life<br /> <br /> Weaver - Forces, Correspondence, Mind<br /> <br /> Wyrm - Entropy, Time, Prime<br /> <br /> <br /> Some of these placements may not make sense but you have to understand the role of each of the Triad. The Wyld simply creates an abundance of 'stuff', popping it into the universe. It creates material stuff, spirit stuff, and both of those create actual life. It could be argued that the Wyld creates forces but that brings me to the Weaver.<br /> <br /> The Weaver gives order to things in the universe. It NAMES them and then freezes them so that they actually persist. To keep the materiae the Wyld creates from disappearing, it must hold them fast and give them form. That is done with forces keeping them together and the idea of correspondence actually placing or DISPLACING, giving them structure, distance from other parts of itself, etc. It's the idea that things are a whole, but they're now separate. The third is Mind. The Weaver cognizes and NAMES these things, giving them a less ephemeral and more permanent form and function. She creates order out of the chaos that is creation.<br /> <br /> Then we have the Wyrm. Entropy is self-evident here and one might think Time belongs with the Weaver, but Time is just <i>duration</i>. It's existence implies an end or a cycle. The Weaver doesn't use Time to keep things in existence, it is Time that will eventually remove them from existence. Entropy and Time (Duration) will break things down and the Wyrm shall eat it into nothing. The most difficult of the spheres I had to place was Prime. It is arguable that all three use Prime for their purposes. I imagined all three of the Triad would each have three spheres that represent one of them. But in the end... I came up with a couple possible conclusions.<br /> <br /> Prime represents the raw potential, that energy stuff that permeates the universe. Perhaps it's there prior to and after the Triad exist. It just IS the universe and either all of them add Prime to their list, or maybe the Wyrm uses Prime to break apart what is static and already exists. Interesting idea because then 'magic' is not 'creation' but it is instead, destruction or the recycling of everything. It embodies everything and it is where everything comes from and where it all ultimately goes. Poetic.<br /> <br /> My favorite is that Prime may actually be used by all three in a sense but it is under the domain of the Wyrm because everything is eventually eaten and recycled... and I imagine that everything is eventually turned into Prime/Potential/Energy/Magic/Mana/Universe/God.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13189-knowledgeseeker","name":"Knowledgeseeker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T12:40:42-07:00","id":1302617,"title":"","content":"By canon the dynamic/wyld spheres are :time,correspondence,mind<br /> weaver/patter: life spirit matter<br /> entropy/wyrm: entropy spirit prime<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> but this is a ridiculous oversimplification. It's more accurate to say that weaver is slightly more attuned to life that mind than to say that she rules it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-04T15:59:39-07:00","id":1302673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302202-the-triad-and-the-spheres-which-could-govern-what?p=1302617#post1302617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By canon the dynamic/wyld spheres are :time,correspondence,mind<br /> weaver/patter: life <b>forces</b> matter<br /> entropy/wyrm: entropy spirit prime</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed that for you. For what it's worth, this is a MRev innovation that hasn't shown up in any other edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302202-the-triad-and-the-spheres-which-could-govern-what?p=1302617#post1302617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but this is a ridiculous oversimplification. It's more accurate to say that weaver is slightly more attuned to life that mind than to say that she rules it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd go one step further: Make doesn't really deal with the Wyld, Weaver, or Wyrm; it deals with Dynamism, Stasis, and Entropy; or with Dynamic, Pattern, Primordial, and Questing. The Triat might get referenced under some Dreamspeaker paradigms; but even there, they're spirits that <i>represent</i> Dynamism, Stasis, and Entropy. They are not, themselves, those principles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T05:17:51-07:00","id":1302787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302202-the-triad-and-the-spheres-which-could-govern-what?p=1302673#post1302673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fixed that for you. For what it's worth, this is a MRev innovation that hasn't shown up in any other edition.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd go one step further: Make doesn't really deal with the Wyld, Weaver, or Wyrm; it deals with Dynamism, Stasis, and Entropy; or with Dynamic, Pattern, Primordial, and Questing. The Triat might get referenced under some Dreamspeaker paradigms; but even there, they're spirits that <i>represent</i> Dynamism, Stasis, and Entropy. They are not, themselves, those principles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the correction,<br /> <br /> At this level though, they are one of and the same. Celestines are supposed to embody what they represent. So Entropy is the wyrm but this doesn't mean there is a big dragon somewhere that you can punch. I think it is seen like that through the lens of lesser creatures(us included)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T08:20:24-07:00","id":1302832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302202-the-triad-and-the-spheres-which-could-govern-what?p=1302787#post1302787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Entropy is the wyrm but this doesn't mean there is a big dragon somewhere that you can punch. I think it is seen like that through the lens of lesser creatures(us included)</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree.<br /> <br /> If you understand 2 and 3 dimensional beings, you know that one thing will look different and/or impossible to the other on the higher dimension. It's because perspective is LIMITED and expands with the higher dimensions you can interact with.<br /> <br /> Let's say a God, debateably a being on even higher dimensions, absorbs another God, right? Kills it, eats it, whatever. Well we might not physically SEE that, but maybe the god being destroyed governs something like Rain or Sky or some such. When that god disappears, maybe down here in our realm it just rains. A lot. And that is the universal expression on THIS dimension of a dying God. Hell, maybe it's a giant flood. But we will NEVER see the reality of what is going on because they are interacting on a scale, with perspectives far greater than ourselves. Maybe the Wyrm is just a force and is disembodied. Has no form. It's just an IDEA or a LAW of the universe. How do you destroy physics? How do you destroy an idea? Kill everone who believes in it? What if someone else a billion years later has the same idea and does that God/Wyrm come back? Did it always exist and just lie dormant?<br /> <br /> Some things in the universe we will never understand until we can perceive higher ideas, higher dimensions. Our awareness must expand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13189-knowledgeseeker","name":"Knowledgeseeker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T11:56:14-07:00","id":1302888,"title":"","content":"The difference is that the Wyrm has an agenda; Entropy doesn't. Put another way, the Wyrm has gone mad and is trying to tear down Reality. Entropy just is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T13:22:50-07:00","id":1302912,"title":"","content":"Prime feels very Wyld to me; after all, Wyld relates to newfound abundance and creation &quot;from nothing&quot; sotospeak.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that every one of the Spheres can be used Dynamically, Entropically and Statically. Entropy could inspire chaos (arguably dynamic), or tear a system to pieces (entropic), or cause a system to run perfectly by removing random chance and decay (static). Prime can break something down into Quintessence (entropic), create stuff from nothing (dynamic) or support a pattern and strengthen it (static).<br /> <br /> You get the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T17:01:41-07:00","id":1302962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1302202-the-triad-and-the-spheres-which-could-govern-what?p=1302888#post1302888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference is that the Wyrm has an agenda; Entropy doesn't. Put another way, the Wyrm has gone mad and is trying to tear down Reality. Entropy just is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Senex would disagree. As of Euthanatos revised and Ascension Senex came to the conclusion that entropy Is devouring and corrupting the world.<br /> <br /> Now, for him entropy doesn't have an agenda, sure, but the unbalance Is clear to him. Ence the mega-ritual he was preparing before the feud with the House of Helekar surged to divine proportions.<br /> <br /> A ritual that on many way resemble a werewolf rite in One of the books, that would require the sacrifice of every werewolf to purify the wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T06:25:26-07:00","id":1303061,"title":"","content":"In my own post-NWoD rewrite (i.e. before perpetually available pdfs became a thing so needed a booklet to give my new players) I did change the spheres slightly (split entropy into fate and death; merged prime effects into all the other spheres... though spirit was it\u2019s primary successor), but the gist of my associations were...<br /> <br /> \u201cMind and Spirit birthed new ideas (Dynamic), those ideas were given form by Forces, Life and Matter (Pattern) and explored through Space and Time (Questing) until they finally succumb to Fate and Death (Primordial).\u201d<br /> <br /> Adapting that back to the standard spheres and the Triat I\u2019d go...<br /> <br /> Wyld/Dynamism - Mind, Spirit, Prime<br /> Weaver/Stasis - Forces, Life, Matter<br /> Wyrm/Entropy - Correspondence, Entropy, Time (I put space and time here because they separate things and break them apart).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}